{
 "concept": "A tall red timber refinery tower is the landmark, crowned with a three-tier pagoda roof. Two wide side workshops step down beside it: a long machine hall with sawtooth north-light and a smaller lab block with a hip roof. A low forge annex with a chimney attaches on the far side. Materials are red timber (red nether bricks style via crimson planks) on both pillar and wall2, dark deepslate base, copper trim and roof accents. Features: pagoda on the tower, crane on the machine hall roof, pipe rack on the hall, chimney on the forge annex, gears on the workshop face, porch at the entrance, balcony on the tower and a bridge-free tight attachment.",
